the Ohio State University is suspending  all fraternities on campus until further  notice the move comes as eleven of the  school's 37 fraternities are under  investigation this semester for code of  conduct violations a majority of the  cases involve hazing or alcohol  Errol Barnett is on Ohio State's campus  in Columbus Erol good morning good  morning  some Buckeyes are stunned by this news  while other students on campus saw this  coming because this is yet another  incident of Greek life being impacted  because of allegations of hazing and  underage drinking now a statement sent  to the chapter presidents from the  University yesterday states that Ohio  State quote will not tolerate behavior  that puts the health and safety of  students at risk indeed this is the  fourth school in two months to ban parts  of Greek life on campus for example on  Tuesday Texas State University  suspended Greek life activities after 19  year-old Matthew Ellis was found dead in  an off-campus apartment alone Monday  Florida State University banned all  fraternities and sororities following  the death of freshman pledge Andrew  Coffey and in September Louisiana State  University suspended its Greek  activities for a month when 18-year old  Maxwell groover died his blood alcohol  level was 0.495 that is more than six  times the legal driving limit and one of  the most high-profile cases is over at  Penn State where 26 paternity members  are facing charges in the hazing death  of Timothy Piazza now here at Ohio State  it's happening at a crucial social time  on campus the last home game of the  season is Saturday students living  inside the fraternities can remain there  while the suspension is in place  sororities remain active Charlie Harrell  thanks
 

